    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **52 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe change belongs in one place: `OwnerEmail.normalize`, the shared email handler used by both create (`ValidateOwnerFields`) and update (`ValidateOwner`), so both endpoints treat email identically.\n\nIn `src/main/java/.../function/owner/OwnerEmail.java` I added a disposable-domain blocklist check that runs after the syntactic validation:\n\n- A `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set: `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n- After lower-casing the email, extract the domain (substring after the last `@`) and, if it's on the blocklist, add `\"email\"` to the errors list \u2014 which the existing `OwnerFieldsValidationException` escalation handler turns into a **400**. Comparison is case-insensitive since the check runs against the already-lower-cased value.\n\nThe `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` test (POST owner with `x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes, and all other existing tests remain green.",
